Skill	craft:review-loop
text	This change touches only documents. So the review is one subagent round. There is no Codex read, because a README is not skill text, and there is no security review. First I commit the change.
Bash	git add README.md && git commit -q -m "docs: correct the npm install command in the README" && git log --oneline -1 && git merge-base origin/main HEAD
Agent	Review README docs change
subBash	git diff 8ce41e1..HEAD; git ls-files
text	The review round found no defect. Next I push the branch and open the pull request.
Bash	git grep -nE '\binstal\b'; echo "check-exit=$? (1 = no typo left)"; git push -q -u origin HEAD 2>&1 | tail -2; cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; Closes #91; ; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the install failed. The README now says `npm install shop`.; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Correct the install command in `README.md` to `npm install shop`; - **Rounds:** Worth first: skipped, documents only. ponytail-review: not installed. Walk: skipped, documents only. Round 1: one review subagent on `8ce41e1..5111f59`, 0 findings. Architecture review: no architecture file or ADR folder; `craft:architecture` can write the first file. Codex read: not run, the README is not skill or prompt text. Last pass: documents only. Security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command; `git grep` for `instal` finds no match.; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none.; - **Declined:** none.; - **Filed:** none. #95 Installing shop by the README leaves the app without the module was closed as a duplicate of #91. Its error message was copied to #91.; - **Docs:** `README.md` is the change itself.; ; 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code); EOF; gh pr create --assignee @me --title "docs: correct the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md
