text	I fixed #91 README: the install command says npm instal, and pushed the branch. The pull request did not open: the `gh` on this machine is a stub and returned `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. So there is no merge question yet.  **What I did** - Fixed `README.md:3`: it now says `npm install shop`. I committed this as `5111f59` on `docs/91-fix-npm-install-command`, in its own worktree. - #91 is assigned to you, and the branch is linked to it. - I closed #95 Installing shop by the README leaves the app without the module as a duplicate of #91. It reported the same README typo. Its one new detail, the `Cannot find module 'shop'` error, is now a comment on #91. - The branch is on `origin` at `5111f59`.  **Review and check** - The change is documents only, so one review subagent read the branch. It found nothing. - There is no Codex read, because a README is not skill or prompt text. There is no security review, because the change is documents only. - The repository has no check command: no `package.json`, Makefile or CI. The closest check I could run is a search of all tracked files for `instal`. It finds nothing. - The repository has no architecture file. `craft:architecture` can write the first one if you want it.  **Docs:** the README is the change itself. No other document exists.  **To finish:** the PR description is ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`, with `Closes #91` and the `## Review` section. With a real `gh` installed and logged in, open the PR with:  ``` gh pr create --assignee @me --title "docs: correct the npm install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ```  After the PR opens, I can run the merge and the follow-up work.
